Permitted use
-------------

The copyright holder and the organisation operating CrossingCount as an
internal service may install and run it on their own computers, and give its
reports to the customers whose footage was validated. Reports are outputs, not
copies of the software, and are not restricted by this licence.

Not permitted without written permission
----------------------------------------

  * giving, selling or lending the program, its installers or its source to
    anyone outside that organisation, including a customer;
  * running it as a service other people reach over a network;
  * publishing the source, in whole or in part.

Both of the first two would also trigger obligations under the AGPL-3.0 licence
of Ultralytics YOLO, which this software uses. Read docs/LICENSING.md before
sharing any build with anyone: it names every component, its licence, and what
each one requires.

